					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "FURTHEST\n\nThe Furtests node takes a collection and tells you which index is the furthest away from the search value.\n\nComputing compound float types like Float2, Float3 and Float4 allows you to weigh your values - telling Wire which element of the type is more important for the calculation.\n\nThis node and it's opposite node \"Nearest\" are great tools for making behaviors.\nYou can calculate which position is furthest to the position of an instance and make changes based on that outcome. "
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
